WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.493
Eco-anxiety is on the rise
and young people

00:00:03.493 --> 00:00:05.748
seem to be some of 
the worst affected.

00:00:05.748 --> 00:00:09.235
Research from 2019
showed that in the UK,

00:00:09.235 --> 00:00:12.888
70 percent of&nbsp;18 to 24-year-olds

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:14.974
were feeling eco-anxious,

00:00:14.974 --> 00:00:18.992
feeling helpless, grief, panic, insomnia,

00:00:18.992 --> 00:00:22.217
even guilt around climate change.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.727
So how do we shift out of despair,

00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:27.699
out of denial,

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:30.471
towards something radically different?

00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:34.237
Think of the one thing you could do.

00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:36.816
The climate crisis&nbsp;is the symptom of many

00:00:36.816 --> 00:00:38.484
interconnected problems,

00:00:39.088 --> 00:00:41.176
from food waste to fast fashion,

00:00:41.176 --> 00:00:42.991
social inequality&nbsp;to how we've

00:00:42.991 --> 00:00:45.219
divorced ourselves from nature.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.606
Every problem requires a solution.

00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:54.127
A&nbsp;solution delivered 
by a someone,

00:00:54.127 --> 00:00:55.472
like you.

